  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Vocabulario legal**",
      "",
      "| Ámbito | Palabras clave |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| Delitos | *theft, burglary, fraud, assault, vandalism, shoplifting, arson, bribery, murder* |",
      "| Personas | *judge, jury, lawyer / solicitor / barrister, witness, defendant, victim, offender, suspect* |",
      "| Proceso | *arrest, charge, trial, plead guilty / not guilty, testify, convict, acquit, appeal* |",
      "| Castigo | *fine, community service, suspended sentence, imprisonment, parole, life sentence* |",
      "| Derechos | *right to remain silent, fair trial, presumption of innocence, legal aid* |",
      "",
      "**Colocaciones**",
      "",
      "- *commit a crime · break the law · obey / abide by the law · bring a case against · stand trial · be found guilty / not guilty · be sentenced to · serve a sentence · be released on bail · pay a fine · file a lawsuit · reach a verdict*.",
      "",
      "**Diferencias importantes**",
      "",
      "- *Steal* (robar cosas) vs *rob* (robar a alguien/algún lugar): *He stole my wallet. · He robbed me. · They robbed a bank.* · *Burgle* (robar en una casa).",
      "- *Lawyer* (genérico), *solicitor* (UK, asesora), *barrister* (UK, representa en tribunal), *attorney* (US).",
      "- *Sentence* (condena) ≠ *sentence* (frase).",
      "- *Kill* (matar) ≠ *murder* (asesinato premeditado).",
      "",
      "**Pasiva en el ámbito legal**",
      "",
      "- *He was arrested, charged and found guilty. · She was sentenced to two years. · The case was dismissed.*",
      "",
      "**Falsos amigos**",
      "",
      "- *Actual* = real. · *Assist* = ayudar (no 'asistir' a un acto: *attend*). · *Legal* (legal) ≠ *legible*. · *Prove* = demostrar.",
      "",
      "**Errores típicos**",
      "",
      "- ✘ *He robbed my wallet.* → ✔ *He stole my wallet.* / *He robbed me.*",
      "- ✘ *The judge condemned him for 5 years.* → ✔ *The judge sentenced him to five years.*",
      "- ✘ *The law says that you have to pay a fine of 100.* (redundante) → ✔ *You are required to pay a fine.*",
      "- ✘ *I assisted the trial.* → ✔ *I attended the trial.*",
      "",
      "**Ojo:** *Evidence* (incontable): *a piece of evidence*. *Crime* (delito en general, incontable) vs *a crime* (un delito concreto). *Police* es plural: *The police are investigating.*",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *verdict* /ˈvɜːdɪkt/ · *jury* /ˈdʒʊəri/ · *burglary* /ˈbɜːɡləri/ · *acquit* /əˈkwɪt/."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "He robbed my wallet",
        "right": "He stole my wallet",
        "note": "Steal + objeto."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "The police is",
        "right": "The police are",
        "note": "Plural."
      }
    ],
